summary:
  A position that went back is read as one that stands.

history:
  The stall timer opens the same address again, and the position starts
  from nought under the same source. With a dead output the new open's
  position never moves, and counted on the old open's movement it would be
  a verdict every twenty seconds.

target:
  package/contents/ui/StandLogic.js

find:
      if (!mem || !_num(posMs) || posMs < mem.pos) {

replace:
      if (!mem || !_num(posMs)) {

expect:
  Killed by tst_standlogic::test_a_position_that_went_back_begins_the_watch_again.
  Line-neutral.
